# Check every text file out with LF on every platform.
#
# Windows runners default to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites the working tree
# to CRLF at checkout. That is not cosmetic here: `schemas/` carries the
# WorkflowAction JSON Schemas whose SHA-256 is negotiated with a host and pinned
# in every compatibility claim, and `templates`-style guidance files are copied
# verbatim into a user's project.
#
# A CRLF checkout would produce a different schema hash on Windows than on Linux
# for the same commit, which would make an exact-pair compatibility claim
# platform-dependent — and the published npm tarball, built from the committed
# LF bytes, would match neither.
* text=auto eol=lf
